	(text "Both footprints sit on the one board, wired to the same nets; only one module is fitted.\nEvery signal into the module is 3.3 V.\nThe module's own 3.3 V output is not used: the board makes its own +3V3A and +3V3D.\nPico 2: 5 V reaches VSYS through D203 (Schottky, net MOD_5V), VBUS is left to USB.\nESP32-P4-WIFI6 (Pico pinout): firmware must set LDO channel 4 to 3.3 V first (pins 21, 22, 24 are on that bank); bridge JP201 for its supply margin. See docs/analogue_board_esp32p4.md.\nTeensy 4.1 (not 5 V tolerant): cut the VIN–VUSB pads before fitting; VIN takes MOD_5V.\nEvery pin has its hole, so standard full-length headers fit; the ones this board does not use are left open."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 24.13 0)
		(effects
			(font (size 1.6 1.6))
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "5a75a5bb-d7a6-559d-9164-cf1a4aaee01a")
	)
